@* The document title for a page whose title is decided at RUNTIME.

   A page that names its title in @Page - or whose master composes one around it - has it
   settled at conversion time, and the converter emits a plain <PageTitle> for it. This is
   for the pages that assign Page.Title instead:

       // BlogEngine's archive.aspx.cs
       Page.Title = Server.HtmlEncode(Resources.labels.archive);
       // and then BlogBasePage.OnPreRenderComplete
       Page.Title = $"{BlogSettings.Instance.Name} | {Page.Title}";

   Nothing read Page.Title, so every BlogEngine page showed the same string - whichever
   master the converter's fallback happened to reach first. Five pages, one title,
   "Account Login", and not a single error anywhere to say so.

   The fallback renders until the page sets a title, and whenever it clears one. Emitting
   Page.Title alone would leave pages that never set it with no <PageTitle> at all, and
   Blazor's HeadOutlet then keeps showing the PREVIOUS page's title.
*@
@namespace WebForm2Blazor.Components

<PageTitle>
    @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Owner?.Title))
    {
        @ChildContent
    }
    else
    {
        @Owner.Title
    }
</PageTitle>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page whose Title, once set, becomes the document title.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Page Owner { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the title was before the page had a chance to set one.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; }
}
